\f0\b\fs32 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project 2: Building an AI Agent for Generative Modeling
\f1\b0 \
In this project, you will build an AI agent that automatically performs generative modeling for real-world datasets. Unlike a traditional benchmarking study, your goal is to develop an automated system that determines when and how generative modeling should be applied to solve a given problem.\
Given a new dataset and a user objective, your agent should automatically determine an appropriate generative modeling workflow, train suitable models, evaluate the generated data, and recommend how the generated data can be used for downstream analysis.\

\f0\b Requirements
\f1\b0 \

\f0\b Task
\f1\b0 \
Your agent should automatically perform the following steps:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Inspect the dataset (e.g., number of samples, feature types, class balance, missing values, image or tabular data, etc.).\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Interpret the user objective (e.g., data generation, imputation, anomaly detection, class balancing, representation learning, uncertainty quantification, etc.).\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select one or more appropriate generative models.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Select appropriate hyperparameters.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Train the selected model(s) and generate synthetic samples when appropriate.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evaluate the quality of the generated data using appropriate quantitative or qualitative criteria.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recommend how the generated data should be used for the given objective.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Produce a final analysis report summarizing the decisions and findings.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 The objective is to build an automated, data- and objective-dependent system that determines whether and how generative modeling should be applied. The agent should make substantive decisions about model selection, hyperparameters, evaluation criteria, and downstream use based on the characteristics of the dataset and the user objective, rather than executing a fixed modeling pipeline.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Generative Models
\f1\b0 \
Your agent should be capable of using the generative models covered in class. These may include, but are not limited to,\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VAEs\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 GANs\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Normalizing Flows\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Diffusion Models\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Your agent does not need to apply every model to every dataset. Instead, it should determine which model(s) are appropriate for the given data and objective, and explain its choices.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Datasets
\f1\b0 \
Evaluate your agent on at least two real datasets. You may use your own data (ideally related to your dissertation), or you can select from the following backup datasets:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 PathMNIST or its variants within MedMNIST\'a0(see a quick summary here:\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medmnist.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 MedMNIST}})\cb1 \
\ls3\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Single-cell RNA sequencing data\'a0(see an example here:\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://scanpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/tutorials/basics/clustering-2017.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 Scanpy 3K PBMC}})\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 You are encouraged to evaluate your system on datasets with different characteristics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

